observations.report:
- **A corrupted `date` is length-checked.** The source tests `date[4]`,
  `date[7]` and `date[10]` with no bounds check (`PepXMLFile.cpp:2004`);
  a shorter value reads past the string. Reported as PEPXML-007.

- **Duplicate identifiers are refused.** The whole-document writer rejects them;
  the streaming path must not be the weaker one. Retained identifier text is
  charged against `WritingLimits::max_native_id_bytes`.
